    "research_questions":  [
                               "RQ1: Can a self-hosted agentic AI workspace operate practically on consumer Windows hardware with 16 GB RAM and a 4 GB laptop GPU?",
                               "RQ2: How do Qwen3 1.7B and Qwen3 4B differ in throughput, resource use, output compliance, and agent suitability?",
                               "RQ3: How reliable are local RAG and persistent vector memory in the tested configuration?",
                               "RQ4: What filesystem boundary does the selected workspace provide for dedicated file tools compared with executable Bash and Python tools?",
                               "RQ5: What deployment and reliability issues appear when running this stack natively on Windows?"
                           ],
    "safe_conclusions":  [
                             "Qwen3 1.7B was substantially better suited to the tested 4 GB GPU than Qwen3 4B.",
                             "Qwen3 1.7B remained fully GPU resident during standardized tests.",
                             "Qwen3 4B required partial CPU offload during standardized tests.",
                             "Local RAG recovered exact and semantic synthetic facts and persisted across a tested restart.",
                             "Synthetic vector memory was retrievable across conversations in the tested configuration.",
                             "Natural autonomous read_file invocation was unreliable for both tested Qwen models.",
                             "The parser and read_file backend worked when the valid textual tool protocol was supplied.",
                             "Dedicated filesystem tools enforced the selected workspace boundary in the tested path cases.",
                             "Bash and Python execution retained ordinary operating-system filesystem permissions outside the selected workspace.",
                             "A shell UI/request-policy mismatch was observed, but disabled-state shell execution was not demonstrated."
                         ],
    "limitations":  [
                        "Evaluation was performed on one Windows laptop.",
                        "Only Qwen3 1.7B and Qwen3 4B were compared for generation performance.",
                        "The standardized benchmark used three runs per model.",
                        "The benchmark used a fixed 4096-token context and 128-token generation limit.",
                        "Agent evaluation used a small controlled read_file task.",
                        "RAG and memory experiments used synthetic fixtures rather than a large real-world corpus.",
                        "The filesystem evaluation was a controlled boundary test, not a comprehensive penetration test.",
                        "Results are version-specific and should not automatically be generalized to later Odysseus, Ollama, model, driver, or dependency versions.",
                        "September benchmark results used different runtime versions and are retained separately rather than merged with the October standardized dataset."
                    ],
